kai: Heads-up from onboarding run — rerank responses inconsistent across SDKs + retry path. One SDK returned "scores" as an array, another wrapped them under "results.scores". Consumer code assumed a single shape and messed up mapping.

viv: Yikes. Which SDKs?

kai: Node and Go sampleapps both show it but with different triggers. Node shows nested "results" when the batch helper compresses small chunks before retry; Go returns flat list unless auth refresh happened mid-batch.

lin: Minimal repro: send 3 queries with ids, force a 401 refresh then a 502 on retry, and you'll see one SDK normalise to {scores: [...]}, the other to {results: {scores: [...]}}. We log the outgoing body as:```
{"queries":[{"id":"q1","vec":[0.1,0.2]},{"id":"q2","vec":[0.3,0.4]},{"id":"q3","vec":[0.5,0.6]}]}
```

omar: That's a pretty bad parity issue. Consumers should never assume a fixed JSON path if SDKs are normalizing differently. Also likely cause: helper code paths for retry/merge apply different serializers.

kai: Short-term fix in sample apps: normalize on read. Example mapping shim (pseudo):
```
function readScores(resp){
  let scores = resp.scores || (resp.results && resp.results.scores) || [];
  // map by id if available
  if(resp.ids) return resp.ids.reduce((acc,id,i)=> (acc[id]=scores[i], acc), {});
  return scores;
}
```

liv: Parity fix ideas: 1) canonicalize response shape in server API (preferred), or 2) have SDK serializer/deserializer modules share a common test fixture. Also add explicit per-item id in response to prevent index reliance.

omar: Filed DE-9001 to align SDK serializers and add tests for auth-refresh + retry + serializer parity. Putting eng-runtime + eng-ml on the ticket.

devex-bot: DE-9001 created and linked to #eng-runtime and #eng-ml.

viv: Extra note: the header refresh path sometimes strips `x-client-batch-meta` which we relied on to reassemble partial retries. Fix there too.

kai: For anyone blocked: patch sampleapps to always map by id (code snippet above) and add defensive checks for both shapes. I'll open a quick PR to onboarding repo.

omar: Also let's add an onboarding checklist item: "validate response shape + map by id; do not assume positional mapping when retries are enabled".

kai: Thanks — resolving this thread for the sampleapp; follow DE-9001 for SDK parity + header retry fixes. :thumbsup:
